# errors with line and column (Phase 16): a runtime error says
# where it failed — `runtime error: <line>:<col>: <message>`.
# The program stops at the first runtime error, so only one of
# the three cases below is active at a time: comment out the
# active one and uncomment another to see its error (the line
# numbers in the expected outputs do not change — a commented
# line is still a line).

# 1. Division by zero: the error points at the `/` operator.
print 10 / 0

# 2. Undefined variable: the error points at the identifier.
#    (Uncomment to try it; expected output:)
#    runtime error: 15:7: undefined variable 'inesistente'
# print inesistente

# 3. Index out of range: the error points at the index.
#    (Uncomment to try it; expected output:)
#    runtime error: 21:10: list index out of range
# let xs = [1, 2, 3]
# print xs[9]
